+# Steel inventory: earlier delivery account recovered; version and custody questions remain
+
+October 28,2026. Existing **STL01–STL04 / B188-H005 / AUD011-AUD016 / SPT01–SPT08 / SR01**. This acquires two previously unacquired primary implementation reports. It does not recover the actual inventory, its native database or any candidate-specific NIST attribution rationale.
+
+## What advanced
+
+The unchanged [July2005 LMDC report](https://renewnyc.org/attachments/content/pdfs/S106_Report_January_to_June_2005.pdf) is **35,544bytes /4pages**; the [July2006 report](https://www.renewnyc.com/attachments/content/pdfs/PA_ReportJuly2006.pdf) is **39,757bytes /5pages**. Both were retrieved from their exact previously exposed URLs, and every page image was inspected. Their full hashes and access records are in [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json). They are agency-hosted report entities, not original inventory enclosures or evidence that every reported action was completed.
+
+The most useful new statement is **July2005,physical3**: it describes an inventory completed and supplied to LMDC in October2004, submission to SHPO, and availability to consulting parties making written requests. Those are separate reported stages. The actual enclosure, transmittal, receipt, accession and copy-request/distribution records remain missing. LMDC, the Port Authority, SHPO and actual recipients are specific source-copy routes; no present possession is guaranteed. IDR02.
+
+The same page distinguishes an expanded catalogue covering collections elsewhere in the country. It also describes four remnants from beneath WTC6 moved to Hangar17. These are scope and update leads, not an established join to W14A/B, C12a/b, FEMA Sample1 or Column79. An item absent from one edition/population is not thereby proved destroyed. IDR04.
+
+## Keep the earlier completion-date discrepancy
+
+| Source | What it reports | Boundary |
+|---|---|---|
+|May26,2005 Port Authority minutes, physical6/printed193|Two-volume inventory,800-plus Hangar17 objects, completed October2004|Previously held; no actual inventory/receipt acquired|
+|Newly acquired July2005 report, physical3|October2004 inventory furnished to LMDC, submitted to SHPO|Contemporaneous program account, not independent recipient acknowledgment|
+|January2011 and January2012 reports, physical5|A similarly titled two-volume inventory,more than800 objects, completed2006|Later repeated account; version/population equivalence unverified|
+
+The October2004/2006 mismatch was already documented. The new report supplies an earlier delivery/access account and more precise retrieval targets; it does not resolve the mismatch or add independent custody corroboration. Revisions, changed coverage, different milestones or an editorial error are untested possibilities. No preferred year or explanation is substituted. Matching titles/counts alone cannot authenticate identical contents. [Source-specific comparison](SOURCE-COMPARISON.csv). IDR03.
+
+The July2006 artifact-review section discusses consultation without specifying an inventory completion date. Its silence does not prove that no inventory existed or was supplied. The held original2004agreement and later inventory references remain separate sources; the new report does not produce the promised July1as-of listing.
+
+## New preservation-document locators, with dates kept explicit
+
+July2006,physical4 reports a **June8 letter**, **Protection Procedure**, **Key Plan**, and SHPO approval concerning north-footprint column protection. It describes planned test blasting beginning **June12,2006** for later construction. Those underlying records, work logs and condition-monitoring results are not acquired. A reported plan is not execution or proven damage. This later work is not evidence of September2001 demolition or a connection to a particular tested sample. IDR05.
+
+Physical1/3 also reports HABS/HAER documentation submitted to SHPO in **August2005**. The actual accession, drawings, photograph keys and complete documentation are retrieval targets; a site-documentation claim is not a specimen-to-building attribution. IDR06.
+
+## Tests and remaining originals
+
+The verifier checks the actual pinned entities, selected source-text anchors and preservation of the two reported completion years. These are documentary/byte checks, not a materials test, historic authentication or demonstration of wrongdoing. All nine new page images were read; older selected page readings are reused explicitly rather than claimed as new. No new OCR or physical examination occurred.
+
+Obtain the actual2004inventory and delivery/receipt/recipient-copy records; the expanded catalogue and update crosswalk; the2006andJanuary2007editions; and the named2006protection/documentation records. For W14A/B and the other selected candidates, native alias/intake/transfer/attribution and preservation decisions remain indispensable. [Exact record targets and contrary outcomes](OPEN-RECORDS.md).
+
+FAA PD01–PD04 outcomes and the telephone, recorder and materials native-input/testing gates remain open. The technical owner’s active NEADS work was read, not duplicated or claimed complete. Earlier sources, conflicting records and shared registers remain unchanged. [Reading scope](READING-SCOPE.json), [claim locators](CLAIM-LOCATORS.json), [checklist](CHECKLIST.md), [verification](RESULTS.json) and [exact additions](TEXT-CHANGES.diff). Publication status is recorded separately; this candidate is not automatically a public push.

